  "title": "Nepal Flash Floods Highlight Himalayan Ice Melting Crisis and Headteacher Evacuation",
  "summary": "Nepal and Tibet faced devastating flash floods and landslides due to a collapsed Himalayan glacier, resulting in over 600 deaths and 2,400 missing people. Nepal's private sectors pledged millions to disaster relief, while authorities mobilised security personnel for search and rescue operations. A headteacher in Nepal evacuated 900 children from a school moments before a deadly wall of water struck their town amid the devastating flash floods that have killed almost 800 people and left thousands missing.",
